105:The CPU expert-fill callback is inactive on this ARM CPU build: it repacks expert tensors into `CPU_REPACK`, so the existing mmap-only fill guard rejects them. The exact requested runs use the default log threshold, which hides the core library's informational inactive message. An additional diagnostic invocation with `--verbosity 4` and `-n 1` confirmed the cause (captured below). The existing Qwen35MoE-only pregate architecture check is not reached because fill initialization fails first; Granite would also be excluded by that check. Enabled readiness and requested pregate stats print once per context even when fill initialization is inactive, with zero counters. No readiness active line is emitted when fill is inactive. This CLI invocation constructs two contexts (two effective-config lines), so c and d each show two readiness stats lines, exactly one per context. These model runs establish output identity, validator behavior, and configured stats visibility, but do not test live fill or join IO. The focused test below exercises nonzero readiness and join paths. No global cache eviction was performed; the small model may already be cached, so resident or near-zero counters in any live-fill run would not demonstrate cold-cache performance.
